{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789333113,"nonce":"Hteky9U4jtO87E+WH5xsZliwnqw=","title":"A host's method told its context, and a found closure called lean","message":"A host binding a class's members as natives has one `NativeFn` per\ntrampoline and no word of its own, so a bound member finds its target\nby the receiver's class on every call, and takes the VM from a\nthread-local since a `NativeFn` gets `\u0026mut dyn NativeContext`.\n`Method::Host(HostFn, usize)` carries the word the host bound it with\nand is called with the VM itself; every dispatch path answers it as it\nanswers `Native`.\n\nA host that has found a method and keeps calling it went through\n`dispatch_method_pub`, which reads the thread's JIT state several times\nper call (`jit_disabled`, `read_jit_ctx`, `jit_depth`, `mutate_jit_ctx`,\n`set_jit_depth`, `call_jit_with_shadow`, `set_jit_context`).\n`call_found_closure` does the same call with the state read once, the\ntrivial accessor fast path kept, and the tier ticked for a body not\ncompiled yet.\n\nCaribou's bridge is the first user of both.","files":null}]}